1
00:00:00,082 --> 00:00:02,552
(Leonard:)I know it only takes
one doctor's finger.

2
00:00:05,487 --> 00:00:06,917
(Amy:)Hello.

3
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:08,593
(Amy:)Hello.

4
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,191
(Leonard:)We should let
you guys talk.

5
00:00:10,193 --> 00:00:11,123
(Howard:)Yeah.

6
00:00:11,127 --> 00:00:12,427
(Sheldon:)You don't have to leave.

7
00:00:12,428 --> 00:00:14,258
Look at me go!

8
00:00:16,264 --> 00:00:17,564
(Amy:)Uh, Bernadette,
you're my ride.

9
00:00:17,567 --> 00:00:18,837
BERNADETTE:
Walk!

10
00:00:23,071 --> 00:00:25,471
(Amy:)How have you been?

11
00:00:25,474 --> 00:00:27,444
(Sheldon:)I'm doing all right.

12
00:00:27,443 --> 00:00:29,773
(Sheldon:)I tried fencing today.

13
00:00:29,779 --> 00:00:31,579
(Amy:)How'd that go?

14
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:34,210
(Sheldon:)It was pretty easy.

15
00:00:34,216 --> 00:00:36,786
(Sheldon:)And I think my background
in "mathletics" helped.

16
00:00:38,453 --> 00:00:40,753
(Sheldon:)Barry Kripke was there.

17
00:00:40,756 --> 00:00:42,026
(Sheldon:)I should let you know

18
00:00:42,024 --> 00:00:44,954
(Sheldon:)that he expressed interest
in asking you out.

19
00:00:46,161 --> 00:00:47,861
(Amy:)Well, actually,
he-he already did.

20
00:00:47,863 --> 00:00:49,833
(Penny:)Okay.

21
00:00:49,832 --> 00:00:51,602
(Sheldon:)But don't get
too attached to him.

22
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:58,020
(Sheldon:)In two years, 364 days,
he's a dead man.

